# oracle: angle_style dipole (docs.lammps.org/angle_dipole.html) on eight dipolar beads (atom_style hybrid sphere dipole
# angle, the torque needs the sphere style): two angles restrain the dipole of atom 1 and atom 4 toward their reference
# atoms (k 2.0, gamma0 60 degrees); the dipoles rotate with fix nve/sphere update dipole. The angle torques and
# forces, the dipole orientations and pe follow the native integration. Native: installed lmp (b332f28).
# oracle-inputs: w235mx_angle_dipole.data
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 1.5e-14, atoms 6.1e-16.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      hybrid sphere dipole angle
read_data       w235mx_angle_dipole.data
pair_style      lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff      * * 0.05 1.0
angle_style     dipole
angle_coeff     1 2.0 60.0
neighbor        0.3 bin
fix             1 all nve/sphere update dipole
timestep        0.002
thermo_style    custom step pe eangle ke
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          25
run             200
